{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0cd9b20539940d0db8ffbf71321b76da8470a2229b97291e003006d92e826f9f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is described as an AI-powered code generation tool for building web applications from scratch through collaboration among autonomous AI agents, framed as a research project."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2faf942efb6b91cd8e50a7cec290f362133bee207d74f5e24500e3ecf92ec7c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers options including --step with values such as specification, system_design, ui_design, development, entrypoint, healing, plus project_name, japanese_mode, review_mode, debug_mode, and plan_and_solve flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3030ceb9593581122bb9f7406b06d188f48282cc8d470748c552c2fa0be20177"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users run the tool via the gpt-all-star command after exporting OPENAI_API_MODEL (e.g. gpt-4o) and OPENAI_API_KEY environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_58b2d576ce96404b84b7495f7d4c20d725b074e7fd01761c4aa3edd885dae170"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Optional LangSmith tracing is configured via LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2, LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT, LANGCHAIN_API_KEY, and LANGCHAIN_PROJECT environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60e57ee88da1cc49be11a4484e2c0b6a3dd004942188454ebdedd59fd6ba0967"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration supports three LLM endpoints selected via an ENDPOINT variable: OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, and Anthropic, each with its own key/model environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9fe0bc7b9379ef830e1b4dcb68fa60e2d1b8e03e1103e877852e157aec43564d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project states its current focus is validating client web applications built with React and ChakraUI in JavaScript, with other languages and libraries not yet tested."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a0b505659649b440f83204076f2e6f0364362e028df25c5769029bfcabfd0d8d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: developers are strongly recommended to run the app with Docker, using make build and make up, then open a web terminal on port 7681 and install dependencies with poetry."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ae70d4c2afc0f07b92447484d8b58741c6d1858019692bf7c232ca7110fd78d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The concept is team-based agent collaboration: a leader is chosen for each step, the leader creates an action plan, and team members work together to complete each task."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d544b75e5a68bddc791af097855d9af31cf7db2952dd2cb55f9996b746cd945b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent team members are configurable by editing the gpt_all_star/agents.yml file, indicating agents are defined in a YAML configuration file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e1cb2761f9d3477992946a9de256b662347a74ffd8a8d3e55623503ded9702ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is distributed on PyPI as gpt-all-star and installed with pip; the project is MIT licensed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ea44d81210badf23f6309926942a8e851cac59cbf1a10a7fae2d69a3e6bb440b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors fork the repository, create a feature branch, and send a pull request; setup uses poetry lock/install, poetry shell, and pre-commit install."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0cd9b20539940d0db8ffbf71321b76da8470a2229b97291e003006d92e826f9f","clm_2faf942efb6b91cd8e50a7cec290f362133bee207d74f5e24500e3ecf92ec7c3","clm_3030ceb9593581122bb9f7406b06d188f48282cc8d470748c552c2fa0be20177","clm_58b2d576ce96404b84b7495f7d4c20d725b074e7fd01761c4aa3edd885dae170","clm_60e57ee88da1cc49be11a4484e2c0b6a3dd004942188454ebdedd59fd6ba0967","clm_9fe0bc7b9379ef830e1b4dcb68fa60e2d1b8e03e1103e877852e157aec43564d","clm_a0b505659649b440f83204076f2e6f0364362e028df25c5769029bfcabfd0d8d","clm_ae70d4c2afc0f07b92447484d8b58741c6d1858019692bf7c232ca7110fd78d8","clm_d544b75e5a68bddc791af097855d9af31cf7db2952dd2cb55f9996b746cd945b","clm_e1cb2761f9d3477992946a9de256b662347a74ffd8a8d3e55623503ded9702ec","clm_ea44d81210badf23f6309926942a8e851cac59cbf1a10a7fae2d69a3e6bb440b"],"crea